Z||000003||terryk||11-17-2000||10:40 PM||||Wouldn't be the first time.....(not you)...<P>Sunbird Turbo or Sylcone (same dash).<P>You'll need a 2 BAR map and the 4 cyl tach needs a mod. Changing the cap won't work. Cut the traces to pins 3 and 11 of the thinfilm resistor chip and solder a 1M ohm trimmer across C3 on the board. Adjust the trimmer for the correct RPM reading. Adjust it at 3000 RPM or greater to minimize the error. <P>It takes some trimming on the face and on the right indicator housing to get it to fit. You'll see. Also, add a 194 bulb in the lower area to backlight the bottom of the tach more completely.<P>With the key on, and engine off, adjust the CT yellow trimmer to 0 boost. Mine was off a bit. The gauge will read -1/+1 BAR (-15/+15). <p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 11-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||11-18-2000||08:28 AM||||Terry,<P>That is one GREAT job! What year of Turbo Sunbird (80's, 90's ?) did you pull the gauge? If found, would you be interested in making the neessary modifications for a fee?<P>Great work,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000005||theogre||11-18-2000||12:19 PM||||That gauge job does look nice. The added light would drive me nuts. I had the SES light on while I was doing some ECM research and that was annoying as all getout. You might want to consider a resistor in line with it to cut the brightness at night.<P>I'd be interested in the wiring for the boost gauge myself, but for a diferant reason. I could use that guage information to get a better reading for some reseasrch I'm doing on the usefulness of the cooling grates in back.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||11-18-2000||12:46 PM||||I turned the CRUISE lamp on with the Tech I so it could be seen. It looks far brighter with the flash hitting it too. It's not that bright. I use unexposed film negatives to decrease the brightness.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 11-18-2000).]||||reg||1
